        "subject": "LU-20720 osd: check the generation around a raw inode parse",
        "message": "LU-20720 osd: check the generation around a raw inode parse\n\nThe OSD scanner parses a raw inode with no lock, so the inode can be\nfreed and reused by another file while it is copied: the FID can come\nfrom one file and the attributes from the next.  The check at the\nxattr read does not see it, since it compares a generation read after\nthe copy.\n\nldiskfs: read the generation before and after the parse.  ext4 zeroes\na new inode before filling it in, so on x86 once any field of the new\nfile is visible the old generation is gone.  If it changed, parse once\nmore, then skip the inode and count it stale.  A copy taken while the\ninode was being zeroed can still show the old generation, but then it\nhas no file type or no change time: parse it once more, then take the\nobject through the inode path.  The xattr read compares the generation\nbefore and after it copies the value.  This holds on x86; on other\nCPUs it is best effort.\n\nZFS: next() reads the generation with the other attributes, and an\nxattr read from the xattr directory checks it again on every outcome,\nso a reused object gets -ESTALE rather than a definite -ENODATA.\ndos_stale is now reported on ZFS.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Icefb159310612fed7ff85d3e23c1cf7054fd7587\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
